  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Des Moines County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSkip to content\n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n \n Des Moines County\n \nElections\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \nDrainage and Levee\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Des Moines County Elections Website.\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find information on past elections or upcoming elections.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nElection Results\n \nElected Officials\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n4\n \n \n\n 2025 City/School Election\n City/School Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n News\n \n\n 2024 Precinct & District Maps\n \n March 5, 2024 County Precinct Maps, Iowa Congressional & House & Senate District Maps are now available \n\n\n\n\n National Association of Counties - News Article\n\n\nAll News\n \n\n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat if I'm still waiting in line when the polls close?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nSo long as you are in line to vote at the time the polls close you will be allowed to vote.  \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nDo I have to vote for everything on the ballot?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nNo. You can vote for as much or as little as you would like; it’s all up to you! \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n\n \n\n \n Des Moines County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated September 23, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n9,291\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n8,532\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n7,792\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n216\n \n\n \nLibertarian\n \n\n\n \n200\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 26,031\n \n Register to Vote\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Des Moines County, Iowa, Elections website at https://dmcountyelections.iowa.gov/.\n\n\n \n\n Des Moines County Courthouse\n\n 513 N. Main St.\n \nP.O. Box 784\n \nBurlington, IA 52601\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Des Moines County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \n \nContact Information\n\n Phone: (319) 753-8232\n \nFax: (319) 753-8227 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
